c_cppr_minus_plain_max": null}, "ci95_seed_t": {"whitewash_plain_vpe": [0.2484316886262692, 0.4802506297035418], "whitewash_cppr": [-0.029477663849991467, 0.11324199022372754], "whitewash_paired_diff": [0.25190437973097946, 0.39301361222509545], "d_mcc_cppr_minus_plain": [-0.063403708924961, 0.018478716169826263], "whitewash_plain_vpe_sd": null, "whitewash_cppr_sd": null, "d_mcc_cppr_minus_plain_min": null, "d_mcc_cppr_minus_plain_max": null}, "ci95_source": {"whitewash_plain_vpe": "hull of the bootstrap and seed-t intervals", "whitewash_cppr": "hull of the bootstrap and seed-t intervals", "whitewash_paired_diff": "hull of the bootstrap and seed-t intervals", "d_mcc_cppr_minus_plain": "hull of the bootstrap and seed-t intervals", "whitewash_plain_vpe_sd": "sample sd over seeds (no interval)", "whitewash_cppr_sd": "sample sd over seeds (no interval)", "d_mcc_cppr_minus_plain_min": "minimum over seeds (no interval)", "d_mcc_cppr_minus_plain_max": "maximum over seeds (no interval)"}, "ci95_unclipped": {}, "ci95_support": {"whitewash_plain_vpe": null, "whitewash_cppr": null, "whitewash_paired_diff": null, "d_mcc_cppr_minus_plain": null}}}, "method": {"tier_coverage": "Training graph of each CPPR network (keeper.laundering.core load, full_graph, train_split with the dataset's tt). Tiers from keeper.credibility.tiers.legacy_bfs (the legacy seeded tiers, moved verbatim from cp_vpe_gpu.compute_credibility_levels). Seeds S0: accounts with more positive than negative in-edges in snapshots 0 to 4. D: S0 plus every account that one pass over the edges in stored order reaches by a positive rating from a member of D (review_tiers.py), checked against legacy_bfs. Active: accounts with a training edge at either end. Late joiners: active accounts first active after snapshot 4; late_in_D_share is the share of them in D. Tier shares are over the active accounts. Every value is a census of the training graph, so ci95 is null.", "single_warning": "revoked_no_expiry: Eq. 8 (keeper.scem.scem.revocation_curve_C), a constant hazard from age lag + L_f on, with no expiry and no closure (the paper's curve and census). revoked_engine_rules: the engine's rules, with the hazard live for H snapshots from maturity and the record closed at A (erlang_Q_P_np and segment_release_increment_np); durable = 1 - revoked. hazard_map: one warning's hazard by the engine's formula (h = L_h xi, nu = softplus(h) - log 2, lam^sigma = lambda_max (1 - exp(-gamma_sigma nu / lambda_max)), gamma = (1.0, 0.8), each witness capped at c = 1). Its revoked fractions are given per channel and mixed by a rating's routing: psi = (0.8, 0.2) for a positive and (0.2, 0.8) for a negative rating, as the engine mixes them. The reliabilities are 1.0 (a fully reliable witness) and the engine's floors, 0.35 up to snapshot 4 and 0.20 after it. witnesses_to_reach: the fewest fully reliable witnesses whose channel-1 hazard reaches 1.9. The constants are the defaults of run_scem_streaming_weights_np. Deterministic, so there is no interval.", "cppr_seed_stats": "Pre-revision runs (superseded by E3): results/laundering/cpgate_count_<ds>_s<seed>.json, seeds 0 to 4, count gate. Whitewash gains: inject_then_erase_whitewash.gain_plain_vpe (Plain VPE) and gain_cp_vpe (CPPR), each a mean over one seed's targets. The paired difference is Plain VPE minus CPPR, seed by seed; paired_t gives its mean, sd, t = mean / (sd / sqrt(n)), df = n - 1 = 4 and the two-sided p. d_mcc_cppr_minus_plain: direct_laundering.d_t1_mcc_cp_vs_plain, the test T1 MCC of CPPR minus that of Plain Erasure.", "ci95": "CPPR seed fields follow ruling R30. ci95 is the hull of two intervals. ci95_bootstrap is the percentile interval of provenance.n_boot bootstrap resamples of the seeds (10,000 by default); the runs keep one value per seed, so the crossed design of ruling R29 reduces to resampling seeds, and ci95_nested equals it in law. ci95_seed_t is the t-interval over the per-seed values with df = n_seeds - 1. The fields are signed, so ruling R31 clips none of them. sd, minimum, maximum, census and closed-form values have no interval."}, "provenance": {"git_commit": "cd9ca69f465dad64c86def4cbf3775037ee4f3b5", "git_dirty": false, "git_status": [], "utc": "2026-10-27T10:39:07+00:00", "host": "kc-sse-ml-rn01", "argv": ["/home/mucbp/PROJECTS/FedUnlearning-Argon/keeper/analysis/defense_extra.py"], "python": "3.10.14", "numpy": "1.26.4", "scipy": "1.15.3", "cuda_visible_devices": "", "n_boot": 10000, "boot_seed": 20261026, "code_sha256": "8b1fa885f400dde048815ba32cd1c8a5513d4d9ca51762f6bc6458561dccdbc5", "module_sha256": {"keeper/analysis/defense_extra.py": "9caf5785710429ee6db2588506a5fb9e5cd1456d0a58851e55d0d5d5c934608a", "keeper/analysis/defense_extra_md.py": "97dca6cdde6e3ce162049263f0ad5caca27be692d7f726d848f81f35f8fc0a25", "keeper/analysis/bootstrap.py": "d591de58208528fa9b5ec2a41003b37517c1ef8ccf17f10070fec5d849fbe5e1", "keeper/analysis/intervals.py": "7b8529f17b8705152559848016242aa1847bd48b3933c3335a1421eaa958612a", "keeper/analysis/laundering_extra.py": "a91e263fd92ec0598b8db01a2a30ab588be271419b9975f7a502754785bdd88a", "keeper/analysis/laundering_extra_md.py": "4ee96c5321a4ed0b06cea44b9a733f7ddb44b3364cec90453769df4ce78b07f5", "keeper/credibility/tiers.py": "c9949fef1ad0020cf635798791cefaae09623d417c85f04acfb01dd0f62595f9", "keeper/scem/scem.py": "e7e2d8a253745651cb1f0d880490357dad72af4a240b5b4fec2d1b1ca75d88c5"}, "inputs_sha256": {"configs/bitcoinalpha.json": "c38a3ffb9ac37d730dcd4218ccb2832690d02bb8d111cccd474e397b9bbb5ac6", "configs/bitcoinotc.json": "e3d7b9728e4a82a5faa452143c22108bd990c6e1ea83ad19b283ce7eb5727757", "configs/wiki-rfa.json": "911b4f9ac8142b44662b2db1bc438fbb9158eafe04e421df753ef35ed10c32b4", "data/cyberdata/bitcoinalpha-rating.txt": "4484de2d10fadd60f80f2667f93980acd4a7ade4a0b664dfcb1c2b08455c9d69", "data/cyberdata/bitcoinalpha.csv": "9b392d2ab6c9c612e9eafbd104de1b69ba8bb7a05293cee52adc8fab50e2130b", "data/cyberdata/bitcoinotc-rating.txt": "309dda5fad163a746b6bb2746cf6175a46f